        <headline>Gale Warning issued September 25 at 3:10AM AKDT until September 26 at 4:00AM AKDT by NWS Juneau AK</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...For the Small Craft Advisory, east winds 20 to 30 kt
with gusts up to 40 kt and seas 7 to 10 ft expected. For the
Gale Warning, east winds 25 to 35 kt with gusts up to 45 kt
and seas 8 to 13 ft expected.

* WHERE...Icy Cape to Cape Suckling out to 15 NM.

* WHEN...For the Small Craft Advisory, from 7 AM this morning to
10 PM AKDT this evening. For the Gale Warning, from 10 PM this
evening to 4 AM AKDT Saturday.

* IMPACTS...Strong winds will cause hazardous seas which could
capsize or damage vessels and reduce visibility.
</description>
        <instruction>Mariners should alter plans to avoid these hazardous conditions.
Remain in port, seek safe harbor, alter course, and/or secure the
vessel for hazardous conditions.</instruction>
